        },
        {
          "height": 32,
          "id": 22,
          "name": "Triple Triad explainer",
          "point": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "type": "npc_spawn",
          "visible": true,
          "width": 32,
          "x": 416,
          "y": 64,
          "properties": [
            {
              "name": "npcId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "triple_triad_explainer"
            },
            {
              "name": "sprite",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "guide"
            },
            {
              "name": "trainer",
              "type": "bool",
              "value": false
            },
            {
              "name": "originalId",
              "type": "int",
              "value": 22
            },
            {
              "name": "dialog",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "I'm here to explain the rules of Triple Triad.\nWhich topic do you want to learn about?\nTriple Triad is a game played with special cards\nplaced on a 3x3 board.\nEach card has 4 numbers on it, one per side.\nThese numbers are so-called stats.\nPlayers take turns placing cards on the board. As\nthey do so, they try to capture and gain control of\ntheir opponent's cards.\nThat's where the numbers come in. If a player\nplaces a card with a higher number next to a card\nwith a lower number, the player captures that card.\nThus, the goal of the game is to gain control of more\ncards than the other player by the end of the game.\nThere are a number of optional game rules you can\napply to individual games.\nThey can affect card stats, how cards capture\neach other, the scoring and the prizes.\nWhen you win a game, you will recive 1 random\ncard from your opponent from their Deck.\nThis also works the other way around: if you lose,\nyou have to give your opponent one of your cards,\nchosen at random.\nYou can change what you win or lose from a game\nby using an optional game rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "height": 32,
          "id": 23,
          "name": "Triple Triad card shop",
          "point": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "type": "npc_spawn",
          "visible": true,
          "width": 32,
          "x": 448,
          "y": 64,
          "properties": [
            {
              "name": "npcId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "triple_triad_card_shop"
            },
            {
              "name": "sprite",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "citizen"
            },
            {
              "name": "trainer",
              "type": "bool",
              "value": false
            },
            {
              "name": "originalId",
              "type": "int",
              "value": 23
            },
            {
              "name": "dialog",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Welcome to the Triad Card Shop.\nAnything else I can do for you?\nAnything else I can do for you?\nHere is where you can purchase new cards for\nTriple Triad duels.\nThe selection grows as you catch and find new\nPok\u00e9mon, so check often.\nAnd, of course, stronger Pok\u00e9mon cards cost more\nthan weaker cards.\nYou don't have to use this shop in your game. It's\njust an example of how the player could gain Triple\nTriad cards. You could implement other ways.\nPlease come again."
            }
          ]
        },
